<%# `Allow: /` next to the disallowed paths is not a contradiction: the longest
    matching rule wins, so `/login` beats `/`. It is there to state the default
    rather than leave it implied.

    The blank line between the groups is for a human — a `User-agent` line after a
    rule already starts a new record — and the second group's agents are stacked
    because consecutive `User-agent` lines share one set of rules. %>
User-agent: *
<%= render "rules" %>
<% @agents.each do |agent| %>
User-agent: <%= agent %>
<% end %>
<%= render "rules" %>
Sitemap: <%= @sitemap_url %>
